[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Core Web Vitals Optimization in Next.js"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Core Web Vitals are a set of metrics established by Google to measure real-world user experience on the web. They focus on loading performance (Largest Contentful Paint), interactivity (Interaction to Next Paint), and visual stability (Cumulative Layout Shift). Next.js provides built-in tools and components out of the box to help developers optimize these metrics effortlessly."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Optimizing Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"LCP measures how long it takes for the main content of a page to load. In a Next.js application, the most common bottleneck is unoptimized imagery or slow server-side rendering (SSR) responses. Use the built-in next/image component to automatically optimize, resize, and serve images in modern formats like WebP or AVIF."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"import Image from "next/image";

export default function HeroSection() {
  return (
    <div className="hero">
      <Image
        src="/hero-banner.jpg"
        alt="Hero Banner"
        width={1200}
        height={600}
        priority={true}
      />
    </div>
  );
}"},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always set the "priority" property on above-the-fold images to hint the browser to fetch them eagerly."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) to serve pages instantly from the cache while updating them in the background."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Improving Interaction to Next Paint (INP)"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"INP assesses a page's overall responsiveness to user interactions by observing the latency of all click, tap, and keyboard events throughout the page lifecycle. To keep INP low, you must avoid long-running JavaScript tasks on the main thread."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use React's transition hooks (like useTransition) to keep the user interface responsive during heavy state updates."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Dynamically import heavy third-party libraries only when they are needed using next/dynamic."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"import dynamic from "next/dynamic";

const HeavyChart = dynamic(() => import("@/components/HeavyChart"), {
  loading: () => <p>Loading chart...</p>,
  ssr: false,
});

export default function Dashboard() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Analytics Dashboard</h1>
      <HeavyChart />
    </div>
  );
}"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Preventing Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"CLS measures visual stability by tracking unexpected layout shifts during the rendering process. Elements that load dynamically without reserved space often cause layout shifts."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always specify explicit width and height attributes on images and video containers."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid injecting dynamic content above existing content unless triggered by a direct user interaction."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure custom web fonts use "font-display: swap" or the Next.js built-in font optimization utility (next/font) to prevent layout shifts caused by fallback fonts."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"import { Inter } from "next/font/google";

const inter = Inter({
  subsets: ["latin"],
  display: "swap",
});

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={inter.className}>
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  );
}"},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"By effectively utilizing Next.js features such as next/image, next/font, dynamic imports, and proper data fetching strategies, you can drastically improve your Core Web Vitals scores, providing a smoother experience for your users and boosting your SEO rankings."}]
